HERE'S A SUGGESTION to LUGs across South Asia.

Please check the following site, and if you'd like some free space for your LUG 
at the IOSN.net network, then you can get it by approaching sunil at mahiti.org

http://www.iosn.net/country/india/organizations/ilug-goa

IOSN has been set up with the mandate of promoting FLOSS, with a focus on Asia. 
They're funded by the UNDP/APDIP and the International Development Research 
Centre (IDRC) of Canada.

Below is one of the sites where you can register you LUG
http://lugww.counter.li.org/groups.cms?&cc=IN

As of now, there are 38 registered from India (some of which are probably 
inactive), though many more have also been launched. If there is a central 
point for identifying active LUGs, it could help build links and spur activity. 
I think LI (Linux-India) also has such a mandate, but probably needs an 
easy-to-fill-in interface. Or am I incorrect on this?

Number of LUGs listed in the above network is:

INDIA (38)

     Nationwide (1)
     Andhra Pradesh (4)
     Bihar (1)
     Delhi (2)
     Gujarat (2)
     Karnataka (5)
     Kerala (2)
     Maharashtra (2)
     Mizoram (1)
     Madhya Pradesh (3)
     Rajasthan (2)
     Tamil Nadu (4)
     Tripura (1)
     Uttar Pradesh (5)
     West Bengal (3)

Somehow Goa's four LUGs seems to have slipped out; we have submitted details, 
so the number should rise to 40+, add unregistered LUGs and minus the inactive 
ones.

Lastly, smaller LUGs in particular are requested to sign-up at the 'Little 
League', a network founded by Sukrit D of Pondicherry. The aim is to build a 
network to share resources and ideas among smaller LUGs and thus help to build 
each other. It would be really nice to have one 'link member' from each LUG on 
board the 'Little League'.

FN
