30. Aug. 2004

Lineox Enterprise Linux 2.1 is compiled from sources available from
ftp://ftp.redhat.com/pub/redhat/linux/enterprise/2.1AS/en/os/i386/SRPMS. 
The only packages that were altered are redhat-logos and anaconda. This 
makes Lineox Enterprise Linux 2.1 highly compatible with Red Hat 
Enterprise Linux 2.1 AS.

Always Current Lineox Enterprise Linux 2.1.007 contains all available
updates including Update 5. Lineox has reserved lower version numbers to
older Update levels and we may make Always Current versions based on 
these if there is enough customer demand because some commercial 
software packages are supported only on certain Update levels.

Main reason for making Lineox Enterprise Linux 2.1 was to create a 
platform on which to build updated packages from source packages 
published by Red Hat, Inc. which continue to be available up to May 31 
2009. Lineox self plans to use these packages to keep some of our 
servers updated, which are still running Red Hat 7.2 based Spectra Linux 
1.1. This is very painless migration because Lineox Enterprise Linux 2.1 
is based on Red Hat Enterprise Linux 2.1 and that in turn on Red Hat 7.2.

Most painless transfer is however using our affordable Update Service on 
existing Red Hat Enterprise Linux 2.1 systems. Lineox doesn't offer any 
other support than package updates, but in most cases that is all what 
up and running systems need.


Availability, Pricing

Lineox Enterprise Linux 2.1 is available as a free download, Always 
Current Lineox Enterprise Linux 2.1.x download quota costs 10 Euros and 
disk images will be available for free with 60 days delay. Update 
service prices start from 30 Euros for a single system 6 month license 
with lower volume pricing available. Updated packages older than 60 days 
are available for free.


Further information

www.lineox.com, linux@lineox.com
Lineox Enterprise Linux 2.1: www.lineox.com/lel21.php
Always Current Lineox Enterprise Linux 2.1: www.lineox.com/aclel21.php
Support price list: www.lineox.com/buysupport.php


About Lineox

Although a young company, Lineox founders have made Finnish localized
Linux distributions ranging from the first one to predecessor of Lineox
Enterprise Linux, which reached about 70 to 90% share of Finnish Linux
retail market. Lineox Enterprise Linux 2.1 is their third Red Hat 7.2 
based version, the first was IT Linux 2002 and the second Spectra Linux 1.1.


