Always Current Lineox Enterprise Linux 3.037 with Update 3 Available

7. Sep. 2004

Always Current Lineox Enterprise Linux 3.037 adds Update 3 compiled
from source packages from
ftp://ftp.redhat.com/pub/redhat/linux/updates/enterprise/3AS/en/os/SRPMS 
(release notes available at
http://www.redhat.com/docs/manuals/enterprise/RHEL-3-Manual/release-notes/as-x86/RELEASE-NOTES-U3-x86-en.html
(x86 architecture) and
http://www.redhat.com/docs/manuals/enterprise/RHEL-3-Manual/release-notes/as-amd64/RELEASE-NOTES-U3-x86_64-en.html
(AMD 64-bit x86_64 architecture)). In version 3.037 the installation
environment was rebuilt, so it offers now better hardware support. 
Lineox has avoided respins because they mean that different versions 
behave differently and that can cause bigger negative effects than 
better hardware support.

The x86_64 release requires either AMD Opteron or Athlon64 CPU based
computer. Some new Intel Xeon and Pentium IV processors that have EM64T
(Extended Memory 64 Technology) should also be able to run this version.


